{
  "slug": "agentsatlas",
  "name": "Agentsatlas",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "AgentsAtlas is a minimal, opinionated end-to-end workflow for Claude Code (also available as Codex skills). Eight slash commands take a project from setup through planning, execution, review, and milestone completion:\n\n/atlas:init, \n/atlas:plan, \n/atlas:execute,\n/atlas:status, \n/atlas:sync, \n/atlas:triage, \n/atlas:review, \n/atlas:complete. \n/atlas:execute \n\nRuns each 3–5-task plan in a fresh subagent (clean ~200k-token context) so quality doesn't degrade across a long run, while a small CLAUDE.md plus .planning/STATE.md and ROADMAP.md keep session continuity without context bloat. \n\nIt also ships 16 development \"discipline\" skills: debugging, testing,\nverifying, refactoring, security-audit, scaffolding, committing, creating-pr, and more enforcing root-cause-first investigation, evidence-before-claims verification, and test-first development. \n\n# Install globally (available in all projects)\nnpx agents-atlas --global\n\n# Or install locally (current project only)\nnpx agents-atlas --local\n\nMIT licensed; no telemetry, no network calls beyond Anthropic, and no bypass-permissions requirement.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **16 skills** and **1 command**.\n\n- **Skills** (16): `brainstorming` (Use before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality), `committing` (Creates quality git commits with conventional commit format), `creating-pr` (Creates pull requests with quality descriptions), `debugging` (Use when encountering any bug, test failure, error, or unexpected behavior - before proposing fixes), `explaining-code` (Explains code with diagrams and analogies), `frontend-design` (Create distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces with high design quality), `mcp-builder` (Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through…), `receiving-feedback` (Use when receiving code review feedback or corrections - before implementing suggestions), and 8 more\n- **Commands** (1): `atlas`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install agentsatlas@claude-community` from `AvinashP/AgentsAtlas`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 16,
    "command": 1
  },
